            "answer_feedback": "Checkmate. The moment the freezing orders drop, the Kuomintang central and local branches instantly transform into refugee camps unable to afford lunch. Those grassroots ward heelers, who are completely accustomed to moving only when cash is involved, turn their backs faster than flipping a page, scattering at a speed that could easily break the Olympic hundred-meter dash record. The pan-blue camp cries foul on television, cursing you as a dictatorial tyrant. Honestly, though, watching a group of people who can barely afford to rent campaign bento boxes and sound trucks throwing a hysterical fit is quite an aesthetically pleasing experience"
