            "answer_feedback": "Unleashing a torrent of media attacks felt highly satisfying in the short term, quickly mobilizing our base on a platform of disdain and mockery. However, this patronizing approach of intellectual superiority triggered an incredibly ironic backfire. Amidst the relentless online ridicule, Han Kuo-yu did not retreat; instead, he perfectly repackaged himself as a 'commoner hero ruthlessly bullied by the massive state apparatus.' His underdog brand grew loftier under our attacks, attracting intense sympathy from moderate voters, the middle class, and even the younger generation, causing the snowball of the 'Han Wave' to roll even faster."
