        "pk": 20994,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 20993,
            "candidate": 67,
            "answer_feedback": "Extending high-profile deference and praise to James Soong on the debate stage executes a tactical diversion, though its strategic impact remains limited by Soong's own marginalized brand and political fatigue. Having run for office so many times that voters joke he is a permanent candidate, this veteran statesman has accumulated significant aesthetic fatigue, and his orange banner has long since lost its former magic to attract massive votes. While your praise flatters the aging politician—prompting him to noticeably soften his attacks on you—astute swing voters and light-blue intellectuals quickly see through your calculations to split the blue camp and remain hesitant. Only a small, highly specific segment of moderate unionists who are deeply terrified of Hung's radicalism and thoroughly disillusioned by the KMT choose to retreat to Soong's camp, siphoning a modest portion of her base but falling short of completely isolating her."
        }
